  <!-- Engineering Principles & Governing Mathematical Equations -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline/80 pb-4">
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-1">{d.principlesTitle}</h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">{d.principlesSub}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm text-body">
      <!-- Equation 1 -->
      <div class="bg-surface p-5 rounded-2xl border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-base">1. Capillary Flow-Focusing &amp; Droplet Pinch-Off Scaling</h4>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
          The balance between continuous-phase viscous shearing stress and interfacial surface tension dictates the transition between dripping and jetting regimes, quantified by the Capillary number (<span class="font-mono">Ca</span>) and Weber number (<span class="font-mono">We</span>):
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface-soft rounded-xl font-mono text-xs text-emerald-400 overflow-x-auto">
          Ca = (&mu;_c &bull; v_c) / &gamma;; &nbsp; d_bead = C &bull; d_orifice &bull; [ (Q_core + Q_shell) / Q_continuous ]^0.48
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Operating strictly within the dripping regime (<span class="font-mono">Ca &lt; 0.18</span>) guarantees narrow monodispersity with a Polydispersity Index <span class="font-mono">PDI &lt; 0.045</span>, eliminating satellite droplet formation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Equation 2 -->
      <div class="bg-surface p-5 rounded-2xl border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-base">2. Supercritical CO₂ Henry's Law Dissolution &amp; In-Situ Acidification</h4>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
          Dense-phase scCO₂ dissolves rapidly into aqueous droplet interfaces according to modified high-pressure Henry's law, generating transient in-situ carbonic acid without added mineral acids:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface-soft rounded-xl font-mono text-xs text-cyan-400 overflow-x-auto">
          C_CO2 = k_H(T) &bull; f_CO2(P, T); &nbsp; CO₂ (aq) + H₂O &hArr; H₂CO₃ &hArr; H⁺ + HCO₃⁻ (pH &rarr; 3.2 – 3.8)
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          The controlled drop to pH 3.4 protonates dispersed insoluble calcium salts (CaCO₃ / CaHPO₄), releasing free Ca²⁺ ions dynamically throughout the droplet core without external calcium bath diffusion lag.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Equation 3 -->
      <div class="bg-surface p-5 rounded-2xl border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-base">3. Egg-Box Alginate-Chitosan Sol-Gel Coordination Kinetics</h4>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
          Liberated divalent Ca²⁺ ions coordinate selectively with homopolymeric guluronate (G-block) sequences on adjacent sodium alginate chains, forming irreversible chelated "egg-box" junction zones:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface-soft rounded-xl font-mono text-xs text-emerald-400 overflow-x-auto">
          2 (-COO⁻) + Ca²⁺ &rarr; [-COO⁻...Ca²⁺...⁻OOC-] (Egg-Box Zone); &nbsp; G' / G'' &gt; 18.5 (Gel Solidification)
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Secondary coating with positively charged chitosan creates a dense polyelectrolyte complex membrane that prevents calcium leaching and resists acidic gastric peptic cleavage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Equation 4 -->
      <div class="bg-surface p-5 rounded-2xl border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-base">4. Colon-Targeted Korsmeyer-Peppas Release Kinetics</h4>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
          Bioactive payload release across gastrointestinal transit follows anomalous non-Fickian relaxation-controlled swelling governed by local pH transitions:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface-soft rounded-xl font-mono text-xs text-amber-400 overflow-x-auto">
          M_t / M_&infin; = k &bull; t^n; &nbsp; at pH 1.2: n &lt; 0.22 (Shrunk Gel); at pH 7.4: n &gt; 0.89 (Rapid Chain Relaxation)
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          At neutral-to-alkaline colonic pH (7.2–7.8), alginate carboxylate groups re-ionize and de-crosslink from Ca²⁺ via phosphate exchange, releasing &gt;97.5% of active payloads directly to the colonic mucosa.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Industrial Technology Comparison Table -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-6">
